-- title:
--   Global additive characters of A_F are dilates of ψ_F
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field (a field of characteristic zero that is a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, with ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_F$), and let $\psi$ be an additive character of the adele ring $\mathbb{A}_F =$ `AdeleRing (𝓞 F) F` with values in $\mathbb{C}^\times$, i.e. a monoid homomorphism from the additive group of $\mathbb{A}_F$ to the units of $\mathbb{C}$. Assume that $\psi$ is a global additive character in the sense of `IsGlobalAddChar F ψ`: it is trivial on the principal adeles, $\psi(\iota(\alpha)) = 1$ for every $\alpha \in F$ where $\iota$ is the structure map $F \to \mathbb{A}_F$; it is continuous; and it is not the trivial character. The conclusion asserts the existence of an element $a \in F$ with $a \neq 0$ such that for every adele $x \in \mathbb{A}_F$ one has $\psi(x) = \psi_F(\iota(a)\,x)$, where $\psi_F$ is `StandardAddChar.stdAddChar F`, the character $\psi_{\mathbb{Q}} \circ \mathrm{Tr}$ obtained by composing the standard character of the adeles of $\mathbb{Q}$ with the adelic trace attached to $F$ through `adelicTraceData F`. Thus every global additive character of $\mathbb{A}_F$ is the dilate of the standard one by a non-zero principal adele.
--
--   This is the classical description, as in Tate's thesis, of the characters of $\mathbb{A}_F$ trivial on $F$: the group of such characters is a free rank-one module over $F^\times$ generated by the standard character $\psi_F$, here in the form that every global additive character is $x \mapsto \psi_F(ax)$ for some $a \in F^\times$. It lets statements proved for the standard character (local components, Whittaker coefficients of automorphic forms, Fourier expansions) be transported to an arbitrary global additive character by the substitution $x \mapsto ax$, and is used in that way by the results on local components and on Whittaker coefficients of cusp forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_ne_zero_forall_eq_stdAddChar_mul_of_isGlobalAddChar.lean

import Definitions.Def_NumberField_AdelicTraceFin

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
